{"name":"Clamshell","hex":"#edd0b6","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clamshell","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shell of a clam.","Any object that, in (literal or figurative) resemblance to the shell of a clam, has a hinge on one edge and two surfaces that close together."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To deform a die in a shape resembling the shell of a clam, as a result of uneven extrusion pressure.","To dig out by means of a clamshell (dredging bucket)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clamshell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clamshell design","blocks":[{"text":"Clamshell design is a form factor commonly used in the design of electronic devices and other manufactured objects. It is inspired by the morphology of the clam. The form factor has been applied to handheld game consoles, mobile phones, and especially laptop computers. Clamshell devices are usually made of two sections connected by a hinge, each section containing either a flat panel display or an alphanumeric keyboard/keypad, which can fold into contact together like a bivalve shell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Clams_on_Sandy_Hook_beaches_-_panoramio.jpg/330px-Clams_on_Sandy_Hook_beaches_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clamshell_design","wikidata":"Q1532758"},{"title":"Clamshell (container)","blocks":[{"text":"A clamshell is a one-piece container consisting of two halves joined by a hinge area which allows the structure to come together to close. Clamshells can be made to be reusable and reclosable, or can be sealed securely, requiring that they be cut open. They are commonly made of thermoformed plastic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/PET-Verpackung-offen.jpg/330px-PET-Verpackung-offen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clamshell_(container)","wikidata":"Q287455"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Clams_on_Sandy_Hook_beaches_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Clams_on_Sandy_Hook_beaches_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Clams_on_Sandy_Hook_beaches_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Clams_on_Sandy_Hook_beaches_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The clamshell form factor is based on (and named after) the hinged design of the clam.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClams_on_Sandy_Hook_beaches_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Clamshell_iBook_G3.jpg/330px-Clamshell_iBook_G3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Clamshell_iBook_G3.jpg/330px-Clamshell_iBook_G3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClamshell_iBook_G3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/THinkPad345C.jpg/500px-THinkPad345C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/THinkPad345C.jpg/500px-THinkPad345C.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATHinkPad345C.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Telefono_cellulare%2C_ETACS_-_Museo_scienza_tecnologia_Milano_09740_02.jpg/500px-Telefono_cellulare%2C_ETACS_-_Museo_scienza_tecnologia_Milano_09740_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Telefono_cellulare%2C_ETACS_-_